{#
  BeMart Shopping complete page — EC-CUBE goShoppingComplete.

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Shopping/complete.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Shopping/complete.twig).

  DATA page (see var/templates/README.md). Markup skeleton, the
  `ec-role` / `ec-cartRole` / `ec-progress` / `ec-cartCompleteRole` /
  `ec-reportHeading` / `ec-off3Grid` / `ec-off4Grid` classes and the
  block structure are kept verbatim from EC-CUBE.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `{{ 'key'|trans }}` -> the ja literal from messages.ja.yaml.
   - `is_granted('ROLE_USER')` — EC-CUBE auth-state runtime. The
     customer-info progress step is shown only for anonymous purchases;
     BeMart's html context has no auth state, so the step is OMITTED
     (the member-checkout path, where it does not render either). The
     step numbering ({{ step }}) advances accordingly — identical to
     EC-CUBE's member-checkout output.

  MISSING BODY FIELD follow-ups (this resource is a thin pure renderer
  — see src/Resource/Page/Shopping/Complete.php):
   - `Order.id` / `Order.orderNo` — the placed order's number. The
     `{% if Order.id %}` block is OMITTED; the body carries no `orderNo`
     (a post-redirect order-id transport is an enrichment-backlog item).
   - `Order.complete_message` — the per-order custom complete message;
     OMITTED for the same reason.
   - `hasNextCart` — whether a second cart remains. Absent from the
     body; the port renders the `goTop` branch (the common case — no
     remaining cart), recorded as a residual in the render test.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% set body_class = 'cart_page' %}
{% set route = 'shopping_complete' %}
{% set title = 'ご注文完了' %}

{% block main %}
<div class="ec-role">
    <div class="ec-pageHeader">
        <h1>ご注文完了</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ec-cartRole">
    <div class="ec-cartRole__progress">
        <ul class="ec-progress">
            {% set step = 1 %}
            <li class="ec-progress__item">
                <div class="ec-progress__number">{{ step }}{% set step = step + 1 %}
                </div>
                <div class="ec-progress__label">カートの商品
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="ec-progress__item">
                <div class="ec-progress__number">{{ step }}{% set step = step + 1 %}
                </div>
                <div class="ec-progress__label">ご注文手続き
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="ec-progress__item">
                <div class="ec-progress__number">{{ step }}{% set step = step + 1 %}
                </div>
                <div class="ec-progress__label">ご注文内容確認
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="ec-progress__item  is-complete">
                <div class="ec-progress__number">{{ step }}{% set step = step + 1 %}
                </div>
                <div class="ec-progress__label">完了
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="ec-cartCompleteRole">
    <div class="ec-reportHeading">
        <h2>ご注文ありがとうございました</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ec-off3Grid ec-text-ac">
        <div class="ec-off3Grid__cell">
            <p class="ec-reportDescription">
                {{ "ただいま、ご注文の確認メールをお送りさせていただきました。\n万一、ご確認メールが届かない場合は、トラブルの可能性もありますので大変お手数ではございますがお問い合わせくださいますようお願いいたします。\n"|nl2br }}
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ec-off4Grid">
        <div class="ec-off4Grid__cell"><a class="ec-blockBtn--cancel" href="{{ url('homepage') }}">トップページへ</a></div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
